{"agent":"bg38","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_under_resume` locates the insertion point with `text.replace(\"# ddflow brief\", lead + \"# ddflow brief\", 1)`. This treats the current heading as the first literal substring anywhere in the text, but the RESUME slice is placed before that heading and can itself contain an earlier occurrence, such as a rendered `### ddflow brief` task heading or a recovered prior brief line; in `\"## ddflow brief\"`/`\"### ddflow brief\"` the substring `# ddflow brief` occurs starting at the second/third hash. Given that input, the reports/contest/Open-workflow-choices block is inserted inside the RESUME content instead of after it, corrupting the recoverable slice and leaving the new blocks above the rest of the resume work. The insertion point should be a structured marker or a line-anchored match for the current H1 heading rather than the first substring occurrence.","digest":"99b4f7981165a084","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_under_resume` places the reports, contest, and Open-workflow-choices blocks with `text.replace(\"# ddflow brief\", lead + \"# ddflow brief\", 1)`. That matches the first substring, not the view's heading line. Given a resume slice that itself quotes the brief heading (this repo's recoverable notes and tests do: `\"## RESUME\\nsee # ddflow brief\\n# ddflow brief\\n## work\\n\"`) plus a non-empty `undecided`, the choices are inserted inside the RESUME section, so the brief no longer opens with recoverable work and the section structure is broken. A resume body with no exact `# ddflow brief` substring drops `reports_block`, `contest_text`, and `undecided` entirely (`if lead else text` never runs when `lead` is non-empty and `replace` finds nothing), so an undecided flow knob disappears instead of moving under the slice.","digest":"f407b32ccbfbeed5","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:304","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:304"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":1538,"diff_sha":"7e5e23962b66e268179cb92045c94f28f388f72d179db5fb94ec1431d67d158c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.7,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-brief-choices-above-resume.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T184946Z-5f163e37.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"4f255a74f56f7bfbe0d3c4eb6b5499f7a9d94145","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py":"100644 97246462767d7eb0466bf5713222956155271315"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_under_resume","ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:304"],"tree_sha":"4f255a74f56f+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e90ab91b0c7d6f32d9d7c4d1e","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":150134,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-brief-choices-above-resume","ts":"2026-11-07T18:50:24.774088Z"}
